meta {
  name: Configure the first page template
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/templates/{{atrapaloFirstPageTemplateId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "action": "GET",
    "url": "https://www.atrapalo.com/entradas/barcelona/monologos/es_ajax/",
    "headers": {
      "Accept-Language": "es-ES,es;q=0.9"
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Page 1 of the stand-up results (40 shows a page) through Atrápalo's
  results fragment, `/es_ajax/` (where `/es_ajax/p-1/` redirects). The
  whole site answers non-browser clients with a JavaScript "Client
  Challenge", so every template runs in a stealth browser (Patchright),
  which reads a page only once it stops reloading itself (ARCHITECTURE,
  browser engines).

  A fixed URL on purpose: it collects page 1's shows and its pagination
  links fresh on every run. A self-feeding list would start from what the
  previous run left (`p-2/` …) and skip page 1.
}
